<title>FINLAND: Finnish producers plan to raise pulp prices - paper.</title>
<headline>Finnish producers plan to raise pulp prices - paper.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish pulp producers plan to follow some rivals and lift pulp prices at the beginning of next year, daily Kauppalehti reported on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It quoted industry sources as saying that there would start to be room for higher prices at the start of next year.</p>
<p>It said that Stone Container of the U.S., Swedish Sodra Cell and Stora and Norwegian Norske Skog had already announced hikes which would lift the price of long-fibre pulp by $50 to $610 per tonne.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 242</p>
</text>
